  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 132 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nIncreased moisture from this system will result in scattered showers \nand storms for the Coastal Plains Tuesday afternoon/evening and \nstretching into the day Wednesday. While we will carry PoPs for the \nAustin metro, the greater chance for showers and storms will be over \nthe Coastal Plains through Friday morning. A second tropical wave \nmay move into South Central Texas Thursday/Friday, but for now, \nconfidence is quite low. Despite any tropical disturbances, the heat \nand humidity will continue and highs will easily climb into the \nupper 90s to around 100 most days through the remainder of the \nforecast period. One positive thing to note is that we may finally \nbreak free of persistent ridging by next weekend as the pattern \nbreaks down.",
